{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in a sprint planning repo. I need to understand the existing context by reading the files in the workspace - particularly the initiative.txt, epic_notes.md, and any documentation in skill_context folder. Then I'll create three files: epic_breakdown.txt, prioritized_backlog.txt, and sprint_plan.txt for a self-service report export feature.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by reading the existing files to understand the context and requirements. I'll start by reading initiative.txt, epic_notes.md, stakeholders.csv, and check the skill_context folder for any relevant documentation.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat initiative.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat epic_notes.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat stakeholders.csv\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find skill_context -type f -name '*.md' -o -name '*.txt' | xargs cat 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered some context but the SKILL.md file output was truncated. I can see the initiative is about self-service report export for end users and administrators with PDF/CSV export capabilities. There are three personas: End User (HIGH priority for PDF/CSV export), Administrator (HIGH priority for audit activity), and Power User (MEDIUM priority for filters and date ranges). The constraints are 2-week sprint with velocity 28 and one developer at 50% PTO.",
  "plan": "Let me read the full SKILL.md file to understand the patterns for user stories, acceptance criteria, and sprint planning. Then I'll create the three required files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | tail -200\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "All three files have been created successfully. I can see:\n- epic_breakdown.txt (6317 bytes)\n- prioritized_backlog.txt (4780 bytes)\n- sprint_plan.txt (5484 bytes)\n\nLet me verify the content of each file to ensure they meet all the requirements specified in the task.",
  "plan": "Verify the content of each file to confirm they contain all required elements: personas with Given-When-Then criteria in epic_breakdown.txt, priority levels and Fibonacci story points in prioritized_backlog.txt, and velocity calculation with committed/stretch sections in sprint_plan.txt.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -60 epic_breakdown.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -50 prioritized_backlog.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -50 sprint_plan.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

{
  "analysis": "The epic_breakdown.txt looks good with INVEST criteria, personas (End User), and Given-When-Then acceptance criteria. Now I need to verify the prioritized_backlog.txt and sprint_plan.txt contain all required elements.",
  "plan": "Check the prioritized_backlog.txt for priority levels and Fibonacci story points, and sprint_plan.txt for velocity calculation and committed/stretch sections.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat prioritized_backlog.txt | grep -A2 'Priority:\\|Story Points:\\|MUST\\|SHOULD\\|COULD'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat sprint_plan.txt | grep -A3 'Velocity\\|COMMITTED\\|STRETCH\\|PTO'\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
